WHAT: compile out the single-instance IPC (QLockFile + QLocalSocket/QLocalServer)
      on __wasi__.
WHY:  it is the ONLY thing in this application that uses QtNetwork -- there are
      zero QNetwork* references in the whole of src/, and `QT += network` in
      qalculate-qt.pro exists for these two classes alone. wk's Qt is built
      with QT_FEATURE_localsocket off; QLocalSocket's headers are not even
      installed in plugins/qt/sysroot, so this is a compile error, not a
      runtime one.
      More to the point, the feature has no meaning here. A wk node IS one
      instance: its own process, its own vfs, its own surface. There is no
      second copy of the app to hand a command line to, and a lock file in the
      node's private filesystem can only ever be uncontended.
      SHAPE OF THE PATCH, and why it is not simply a deletion: serverNewConnection()
      and socketReadyRead() keep their declarations and their (now empty)
      definitions. moc does not see __wasi__ -- it is a compiler builtin, not a
      -D that AUTOMOC forwards -- so a header guarded on it would still emit
      metaobject entries for slots the compiler had removed, and the app would
      fail to link with undefined qt_static_metacall targets. The member
      pointers need no guard at all: qalculatewindow.h only forward-declares
      `class QLocalSocket;`.
UPSTREAM: not-as-is. Upstream would want a configure-time switch (they already
      have `--new-instance`), not an #ifdef on a platform macro.
